On Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:50:40 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> This is the flip side of the earlier question. Why use IMAP as the
> transfer protocol?

On the client side it comes down to what mbsync gives lab-claude: it
fetches only new messages by UID, keeps its own sync state, and
never writes to the server. notmuch then indexes a plain local
maildir, so reading and searching keep working when lab-mail is
down. Any transfer that lands a maildir locally would serve notmuch
equally well; the choice rests on the server side.

I answered that in full on 5/6, in "Re: [PATCH v8 5/6]
jails/instances/lab-mail: Serve the mirror over IMAP with Dovecot".
In short, I recommend keeping IMAP, with rsync over ssh and rrsync
as the alternative if you would rather drop Dovecot. 6/6 follows
whichever you choose.
